    "background_story": "Clayton was a brilliant mechanic with a passion for restoring classic cars. He spent most of his days tinkering with engines and transmissions, but his true expertise lay in inspecting and repairing the often-overlooked undercarriage. With a keen eye for detail, Clayton could spot a rusty suspension component or a worn-out axle from a mile away. His workshop, 'Clayton's Classics,' became the go-to destination for car enthusiasts seeking meticulous undercarriage repairs. One day, a rare 1969 Mustang came into his shop, its undercarriage in shambles. Clayton worked tirelessly to restore the car to its former glory, earning the admiration of the car's owner and cementing his reputation as the undercarriage whisperer.",
